# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial reproduces the error-detected, approximate preparation of a W state by using dynamic circuits, as presented in [Smith, Pokharel, Maurya, Takita, \"Resilience Beyond the Light Cone: Error-Detected Primitives for Practical Dynamic Circuits\" (2026)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08925) [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menghasilkan semula penyediaan anggaran bagi keadaan W dengan pengesanan ralat menggunakan litar dinamik, seperti yang dibentangkan dalam [Smith, Pokharel, Maurya, Takita, \"Resilience Beyond the Light Cone: Error-Detected Primitives for Practical Dynamic Circuits\" (2026)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08925) [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The approach is an adaptation of the algorithm presented in [Piroli, Styliaris, Cirac, \"Approximating many-body quantum states with quantum circuits and measurements\" (2024)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.07604) [\\[2\\]](#references), upgraded with the *Distributed Control Error Detection* (DisCo ED) scheme of [Smith et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08925) The paper runs the protocol on a heavy-hex processor. Here, the protocol runs on the square lattice of a Nighthawk processor. The noisy simulation reproduces its main finding: both DisCo ED checks improve the prepared state compared with no error detection, and the implicit check gives the best state. On hardware at $n = 10$, the idle time during the feedforward limits how much error detection can recover, as discussed after the hardware results.\n"
msgstr "Pendekatan ini ialah adaptasi algoritma yang dibentangkan dalam [Piroli, Styliaris, Cirac, \"Approximating many-body quantum states with quantum circuits and measurements\" (2024)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.07604) [\\[2\\]](#references), yang dinaik taraf dengan skema *Distributed Control Error Detection* (DisCo ED) daripada [Smith et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08925) Kertas kerja itu menjalankan protokol pada pemproses heavy-hex. Di sini, protokol berjalan pada kekisi segi empat sama bagi pemproses Nighthawk. Simulasi berhingar menghasilkan semula penemuan utamanya: kedua-dua semakan DisCo ED memperbaik keadaan yang disediakan berbanding tanpa pengesanan ralat, dan semakan tersirat memberikan keadaan terbaik. Pada perkakasan dengan $n = 10$, masa melahu semasa feedforward mengehadkan sejauh mana pengesanan ralat dapat memulihkan, seperti yang dibincangkan selepas keputusan perkakasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following sections describe the ingredients of this tutorial in detail.\n"
msgstr "Bahagian berikut menerangkan bahan-bahan tutorial ini secara terperinci.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The W state {#the-w-state}"
msgstr "Keadaan W {#the-w-state}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The $n$-qubit W state is the equal superposition of all states with exactly one excitation,\n"
msgstr "Keadaan W $n$-qubit ialah superposisi sama rata bagi semua keadaan dengan tepat satu pengujaan,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|W_n\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}\\Big(|10\\cdots0\\rangle + |01\\cdots0\\rangle + \\cdots + |00\\cdots1\\rangle\\Big) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}\\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}|e_j\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|W_n\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}\\Big(|10\\cdots0\\rangle + |01\\cdots0\\rangle + \\cdots + |00\\cdots1\\rangle\\Big) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}\\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}|e_j\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $|e_j\\rangle$ has a single $|1\\rangle$ on qubit $j$. Unlike the GHZ state, its entanglement survives the loss of any one qubit. This tutorial characterizes the prepared state with two simple observables.\n"
msgstr "dengan $|e_j\\rangle$ mempunyai satu $|1\\rangle$ pada qubit $j$. Tidak seperti keadaan GHZ, keterjalinannya bertahan apabila mana-mana satu qubit hilang. Tutorial ini mencirikan keadaan yang disediakan dengan dua cerapan ringkas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Hamming-weight distribution.** Measure every qubit in the $Z$ basis and count the number of 1s, $w$. A perfect W state gives $P(w=1) = 1$.\n"
msgstr "**Taburan berat Hamming.** Ukur setiap qubit dalam asas $Z$ dan kira bilangan 1, $w$. Keadaan W yang sempurna memberikan $P(w=1) = 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Coherence.** $P(w=1)=1$ alone does not certify a W state: an incoherent mixture $\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_j |e_j\\rangle\\langle e_j|$, or a superposition $\\sum_j \\pm|e_j\\rangle$ with random signs, also has $P(w=1)=1$. To probe the relative phases, use\n"
msgstr "**Koheren.** $P(w=1)=1$ sahaja tidak mengesahkan keadaan W: campuran tidak koheren $\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_j |e_j\\rangle\\langle e_j|$, atau superposisi $\\sum_j \\pm|e_j\\rangle$ dengan tanda rawak, juga mempunyai $P(w=1)=1$. Untuk menyiasat fasa relatif, gunakan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C = \\frac{n}{4}\\cdot\\frac{1}{n(n-1)}\\sum_{i\\neq j}\\big\\langle X_iX_j + Y_iY_j\\big\\rangle .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C = \\frac{n}{4}\\cdot\\frac{1}{n(n-1)}\\sum_{i\\neq j}\\big\\langle X_iX_j + Y_iY_j\\big\\rangle .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operator $X_iX_j + Y_iY_j = 2(\\sigma_i^+\\sigma_j^- + \\sigma_i^-\\sigma_j^+)$ moves an excitation between qubits $i$ and $j$. For a state $\\sum_j c_j|e_j\\rangle$ it gives $\\langle X_iX_j + Y_iY_j\\rangle = 4\\,\\mathrm{Re}(c_i^*c_j)$, so $C = 1$ for $|W_n\\rangle$, $C = 0$ for the incoherent mixture, and random signs push $C$ toward zero. Measuring $C$ takes only two extra circuits: one with every W qubit measured in the $X$ basis, and one in the $Y$ basis.\n"
msgstr "Pengendali $X_iX_j + Y_iY_j = 2(\\sigma_i^+\\sigma_j^- + \\sigma_i^-\\sigma_j^+)$ menggerakkan satu pengujaan antara qubit $i$ dan $j$. Bagi keadaan $\\sum_j c_j|e_j\\rangle$ ia memberikan $\\langle X_iX_j + Y_iY_j\\rangle = 4\\,\\mathrm{Re}(c_i^*c_j)$, jadi $C = 1$ bagi $|W_n\\rangle$, $C = 0$ bagi campuran tidak koheren, dan tanda rawak menolak $C$ ke arah sifar. Mengukur $C$ hanya memerlukan dua litar tambahan: satu dengan setiap qubit W diukur dalam asas $X$, dan satu dalam asas $Y$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamic circuits {#dynamic-circuits}"
msgstr "Litar dinamik {#dynamic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A unitary circuit of nearest-neighbor gates spreads correlations only within a *light cone* that grows by a fixed distance per layer. Preparing a long-range entangled state such as a GHZ or W state on a line of $n$ qubits therefore takes a depth that grows with $n$. Dynamic circuits, which use mid-circuit measurements and classical feedforward, get around this limit: measurement outcomes are processed classically and sent to qubits anywhere on the chip, in a time that does not depend on distance.\n"
msgstr "Litar uniter bagi gate jiran terdekat menyebarkan korelasi hanya dalam *kon cahaya* yang membesar dengan jarak tetap bagi setiap lapisan. Menyediakan keadaan terjalin jarak jauh seperti keadaan GHZ atau W pada satu garis $n$ qubit oleh itu memerlukan kedalaman yang bertambah dengan $n$. Litar dinamik, yang menggunakan pengukuran pertengahan litar dan feedforward klasik, mengatasi had ini: hasil pengukuran diproses secara klasik dan dihantar kepada qubit di mana-mana pada cip, dalam masa yang tidak bergantung pada jarak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A paradigmatic example is the constant-depth GHZ state (see the [long-range entanglement tutorial](/tutorials/long-range-entanglement) and [\\[3\\]](#references)). The protocol splits the line into small *patches* and prepares small GHZ states on each patch in parallel. It then *fuses* neighboring patches by measuring the parity $Z_aZ_b$ across each boundary. Outcome $m_k = 1$ means the two patches disagree. Applying $X$ to every qubit of patch $k$ whenever the cumulative parity $m_1 \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus m_k$ is 1 fixes every disagreement in a single round of feedforward. In this circuit, each measured qubit is then reset and re-entangled with its own patch, so all $n$ qubits end up in\n"
msgstr "Contoh paradigma ialah keadaan GHZ berkedalaman tetap (lihat [tutorial keterjalinan jarak jauh](/tutorials/long-range-entanglement) dan [\\[3\\]](#references)). Protokol ini membahagikan garis kepada *tampalan* kecil dan menyediakan keadaan GHZ kecil pada setiap tampalan secara selari. Kemudian ia *menggabungkan* tampalan berjiran dengan mengukur pariti $Z_aZ_b$ merentasi setiap sempadan. Hasil $m_k = 1$ bermakna kedua-dua tampalan tidak sepakat. Menggunakan $X$ pada setiap qubit tampalan $k$ apabila pariti kumulatif $m_1 \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus m_k$ ialah 1 membetulkan setiap ketidaksepakatan dalam satu pusingan feedforward. Dalam litar ini, setiap qubit yang diukur kemudian ditetapkan semula dan dijalin semula dengan tampalannya sendiri, supaya semua $n$ qubit berakhir dalam\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\mathrm{GHZ}\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\big(|0\\cdots0\\rangle + |1\\cdots1\\rangle\\big),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\mathrm{GHZ}\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\big(|0\\cdots0\\rangle + |1\\cdots1\\rangle\\big),\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "in a depth that does not depend on $n$.\n"
msgstr "dalam kedalaman yang tidak bergantung pada $n$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Approximate preparation of the W state {#approximate-preparation-of-the-w-state}"
msgstr "Penyediaan anggaran keadaan W {#approximate-preparation-of-the-w-state}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The idea of the W-state-preparation protocol of Ref. [\\[2\\]](#references) is to start from a product state that overlaps strongly with $|W\\rangle$, then *project* away the unwanted components. Rotating every qubit with $R_Y(\\theta)$, where $\\sin^2(\\theta/2) = p$, gives\n"
msgstr "Idea protokol penyediaan keadaan W dalam Rujuk. [\\[2\\]](#references) ialah bermula daripada keadaan hasil darab yang bertindih kuat dengan $|W\\rangle$, kemudian *memproyeksikan* keluar komponen yang tidak dikehendaki. Memutarkan setiap qubit dengan $R_Y(\\theta)$, dengan $\\sin^2(\\theta/2) = p$, memberikan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\phi\\rangle = \\bigotimes_{j}\\Big(\\sqrt{1-p}\\,|0\\rangle + \\sqrt{p}\\,|1\\rangle\\Big) = \\sum_{k=0}^{n}\\sqrt{P_k}\\,|D_k\\rangle, \\qquad P_k = \\binom{n}{k}p^k(1-p)^{n-k},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\phi\\rangle = \\bigotimes_{j}\\Big(\\sqrt{1-p}\\,|0\\rangle + \\sqrt{p}\\,|1\\rangle\\Big) = \\sum_{k=0}^{n}\\sqrt{P_k}\\,|D_k\\rangle, \\qquad P_k = \\binom{n}{k}p^k(1-p)^{n-k},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $|D_k\\rangle$ is the uniform superposition of all weight-$k$ states (the Dicke state, with $|D_1\\rangle = |W\\rangle$). For small $p$, almost all of the weight is in $k=0$ and $k=1$. Projecting onto odd parity with $\\Pi_{\\rm odd} = (1 - Z^{\\otimes n})/2$ removes $k = 0, 2, 4, \\ldots$ and leaves\n"
msgstr "dengan $|D_k\\rangle$ ialah superposisi seragam bagi semua keadaan berat-$k$ (keadaan Dicke, dengan $|D_1\\rangle = |W\\rangle$). Bagi $p$ kecil, hampir semua berat berada pada $k=0$ dan $k=1$. Memproyeksikan pada pariti ganjil dengan $\\Pi_{\\rm odd} = (1 - Z^{\\otimes n})/2$ membuang $k = 0, 2, 4, \\ldots$ dan meninggalkan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_{\\rm odd}|\\phi\\rangle \\propto \\sqrt{P_1}\\,|W\\rangle + \\sqrt{P_3}\\,|D_3\\rangle + \\cdots .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_{\\rm odd}|\\phi\\rangle \\propto \\sqrt{P_1}\\,|W\\rangle + \\sqrt{P_3}\\,|D_3\\rangle + \\cdots .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The projection succeeds with probability $r_s = \\sum_{k\\,\\rm odd}P_k = \\big[1 - (1-2p)^n\\big]/2$, and the fidelity with the W state is $F = P_1/r_s$. Choosing $p = \\delta/n$, for large $n$\n"
msgstr "Proyeksi berjaya dengan kebarangkalian $r_s = \\sum_{k\\,\\rm odd}P_k = \\big[1 - (1-2p)^n\\big]/2$, dan kesetiaan dengan keadaan W ialah $F = P_1/r_s$. Dengan memilih $p = \\delta/n$, bagi $n$ besar\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"F \\to \\frac{\\delta}{\\sinh\\delta} \\approx 1 - \\frac{\\delta^2}{6}, \\qquad r_s \\to \\frac{1 - e^{-2\\delta}}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"F \\to \\frac{\\delta}{\\sinh\\delta} \\approx 1 - \\frac{\\delta^2}{6}, \\qquad r_s \\to \\frac{1 - e^{-2\\delta}}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Neither depends on $n$, so the cost of the protocol does not grow with system size. The parameter $\\delta$ trades fidelity against success rate. This tutorial uses $\\delta = 0.3$, which gives $F \\approx 0.985$ and $r_s \\approx 0.23$. The small remaining infidelity comes from higher odd-weight components.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-duanya tidak bergantung pada $n$, jadi kos protokol tidak bertambah dengan saiz sistem. Parameter $\\delta$ menukar ganti kesetiaan dengan kadar kejayaan. Tutorial ini menggunakan $\\delta = 0.3$, yang memberikan $F \\approx 0.985$ dan $r_s \\approx 0.23$. Ketidaksetiaan kecil yang tinggal datang daripada komponen berat ganjil yang lebih tinggi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Single-ancilla projection.** One way to apply $\\Pi_{\\rm odd}$ is a Hadamard test. Prepare an ancilla in $|+\\rangle$, apply $CZ$ between the ancilla and every system qubit (a controlled-$Z^{\\otimes n}$), and measure the ancilla in the $X$ basis:\n"
msgstr "**Proyeksi ancilla tunggal.** Satu cara untuk menggunakan $\\Pi_{\\rm odd}$ ialah ujian Hadamard. Sediakan ancilla dalam $|+\\rangle$, gunakan $CZ$ antara ancilla dan setiap qubit sistem (satu $Z^{\\otimes n}$ terkawal), dan ukur ancilla dalam asas $X$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(|0\\rangle|\\phi\\rangle + |1\\rangle Z^{\\otimes n}|\\phi\\rangle\\Big) = |+\\rangle\\,\\frac{1 + Z^{\\otimes n}}{2}|\\phi\\rangle + |-\\rangle\\,\\frac{1 - Z^{\\otimes n}}{2}|\\phi\\rangle .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(|0\\rangle|\\phi\\rangle + |1\\rangle Z^{\\otimes n}|\\phi\\rangle\\Big) = |+\\rangle\\,\\frac{1 + Z^{\\otimes n}}{2}|\\phi\\rangle + |-\\rangle\\,\\frac{1 - Z^{\\otimes n}}{2}|\\phi\\rangle .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Outcome \"$-$\" heralds the odd sector. The catch is that a single ancilla must interact with all $n$ qubits, requiring a circuit depth proportional to $n$.\n"
msgstr "Hasil \"$-$\" mengisyaratkan sektor ganjil. Masalahnya ialah satu ancilla mesti berinteraksi dengan kesemua $n$ qubit, yang memerlukan kedalaman litar berkadar dengan $n$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Distributed control.** Replace the single ancilla with an $n$-qubit GHZ state prepared via dynamic circuits, and place the GHZ qubit $g_j$ next to W qubit $w_j$. The GHZ state behaves as one *logical* qubit, with $|\\bar 0\\rangle = |0\\cdots0\\rangle$, $|\\bar 1\\rangle = |1\\cdots1\\rangle$, and logical operator $\\bar X = X^{\\otimes n}$. The controlled-$Z^{\\otimes n}$ becomes $CZ(g_j, w_j)$ on every pair at once, a single layer of gates. Measuring $\\bar X$ means measuring every GHZ qubit in the $X$ basis and multiplying the outcomes, so an odd number of 1s heralds success. Every step now has constant depth. On a square lattice, the GHZ line and the W line form a *ladder*: two rows of $n$ qubits joined by $n$ rungs.\n"
msgstr "**Kawalan teragih.** Gantikan ancilla tunggal dengan keadaan GHZ $n$-qubit yang disediakan melalui litar dinamik, dan letakkan qubit GHZ $g_j$ bersebelahan qubit W $w_j$. Keadaan GHZ berkelakuan sebagai satu qubit *logik*, dengan $|\\bar 0\\rangle = |0\\cdots0\\rangle$, $|\\bar 1\\rangle = |1\\cdots1\\rangle$, dan pengendali logik $\\bar X = X^{\\otimes n}$. $Z^{\\otimes n}$ terkawal menjadi $CZ(g_j, w_j)$ pada setiap pasangan serentak, satu lapisan gate. Mengukur $\\bar X$ bermakna mengukur setiap qubit GHZ dalam asas $X$ dan mendarabkan hasilnya, jadi bilangan 1 yang ganjil mengisyaratkan kejayaan. Setiap langkah kini mempunyai kedalaman tetap. Pada kekisi segi empat sama, garis GHZ dan garis W membentuk *tangga*: dua baris $n$ qubit yang disambung oleh $n$ anak tangga.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Ladder layout of the GHZ line and the W line on the square lattice](/docs/images/tutorials/error-detected-w-state/w-state-ladder.avif) *(a) The GHZ line and the W line occupy two neighboring rows of the square lattice and are joined by $CZ(g_j, w_j)$ rungs. (b) The GHZ line alone. The staggered prep patches (shaded) are fused by mid-circuit measurements at the marked boundaries. Each boundary falls inside one of the DisCo ED detection pairs (check $c$, root $r$), so a faulty fusion is detected.*\n"
msgstr "![Ladder layout of the GHZ line and the W line on the square lattice](/docs/images/tutorials/error-detected-w-state/w-state-ladder.avif) *(a) The GHZ line and the W line occupy two neighboring rows of the square lattice and are joined by $CZ(g_j, w_j)$ rungs. (b) The GHZ line alone. The staggered prep patches (shaded) are fused by mid-circuit measurements at the marked boundaries. Each boundary falls inside one of the DisCo ED detection pairs (check $c$, root $r$), so a faulty fusion is detected.*\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "DisCo ED {#disco-ed}"
msgstr "DisCo ED {#disco-ed}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While the distributed control technique reduces the procedure to a constant depth circuit, it does not come for free.  It requires $n$ ancillas and, more importantly, $\\lceil n/2 \\rceil - 1$ mid-circuit measurements. Readout error is typically slightly worse than two-qubit gate error on superconducting devices, so implementing this strategy can introduce significant noise. Additional challenges include the fact that the GHZ qubits sit idle during the mid-circuit measurements and feedforward, making them susceptible to relaxation and dephasing errors, and the final $\\bar X$ readout requires measurement of an $n$-qubit operator.\n"
msgstr "Walaupun teknik kawalan teragih mengurangkan prosedur kepada litar berkedalaman tetap, ia tidak percuma. Ia memerlukan $n$ ancilla dan, yang lebih penting, $\\lceil n/2 \\rceil - 1$ pengukuran pertengahan litar. Ralat bacaan biasanya sedikit lebih teruk daripada ralat gate dua-qubit pada peranti superkonduktor, jadi melaksanakan strategi ini boleh memperkenalkan hingar yang ketara. Cabaran tambahan termasuk hakikat bahawa qubit GHZ melahu semasa pengukuran pertengahan litar dan feedforward, menjadikannya mudah terdedah kepada ralat relaksasi dan nyahfasa, dan bacaan $\\bar X$ akhir memerlukan pengukuran pengendali $n$-qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To dig further into the impact of noise, consider the effect of each type of error on the GHZ state throughout this protocol:\n"
msgstr "Untuk mendalami kesan hingar, pertimbangkan kesan setiap jenis ralat pada keadaan GHZ sepanjang protokol ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Bit flips:** The CZ layer turns $X_{g_j}$ (with $g_j$ denoting the $j$-th GHZ qubit) into $X_{g_j}Z_{w_j}$ (with $w_j$ denoting the $j$-th W state qubit), so a bit flip on $g_j$ applies $Z$ to $w_j$. Because $X_{g_j}$ commutes with $\\bar X$, the herald is unaffected, and the error flips the sign of one W amplitude. The Hamming weight is blind to this, but $C$ drops.\n"
msgstr "**Balikan bit:** Lapisan CZ mengubah $X_{g_j}$ (dengan $g_j$ menandakan qubit GHZ ke-$j$) menjadi $X_{g_j}Z_{w_j}$ (dengan $w_j$ menandakan qubit keadaan W ke-$j$), jadi balikan bit pada $g_j$ menggunakan $Z$ pada $w_j$. Oleh sebab $X_{g_j}$ kalis tukar tertib dengan $\\bar X$, isyarat tidak terjejas, dan ralat membalikkan tanda satu amplitud W. Berat Hamming buta terhadap hal ini, tetapi $C$ menurun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Fusion readout errors:** Because the parity of fusion mid-circuit measurement outcomes determines the pattern of X-corrections applied via feedforward when preparing the GHZ state, a wrong fusion outcome creates a pattern of bit flip errors called a *domain wall*. Depending on how the feedforward corrections are applied, a domain wall between sites $j$ and $j+1$ produces a bit-flip error on all GHZ qubits to the left (or right) of the domain wall. The impact of these bit flip errors on the state is as discussed above.\n"
msgstr "**Ralat bacaan gabungan:** Oleh sebab pariti hasil pengukuran pertengahan litar gabungan menentukan corak pembetulan X yang dikenakan melalui feedforward semasa menyediakan keadaan GHZ, hasil gabungan yang salah mencipta corak ralat balikan bit yang dipanggil *dinding domain*. Bergantung pada cara pembetulan feedforward dikenakan, dinding domain antara tapak $j$ dan $j+1$ menghasilkan ralat balikan bit pada semua qubit GHZ di sebelah kiri (atau kanan) dinding domain. Kesan ralat balikan bit ini terhadap keadaan adalah seperti yang dibincangkan di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Phase flips and readout errors** on the GHZ qubits flip the herald, so the protocol accepts the even-parity sector by mistake. These show up as weight 0 and weight 2 in the Hamming-weight distribution.\n"
msgstr "**Balikan fasa dan ralat bacaan** pada qubit GHZ membalikkan isyarat, jadi protokol tersilap menerima sektor pariti genap. Ini muncul sebagai berat 0 dan berat 2 dalam taburan berat Hamming.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "DisCo ED starts from the observation that the GHZ state is a repetition code: its stabilizers are $Z_jZ_{j+1}$ and its logical operator is $\\bar X$. A plain readout measures each qubit in the $X$ basis, which reveals $\\bar X$ but by gathering independent pieces of information that are not useful to the protocol (that is, each individual $X$). The idea of DisCo ED is to replace these \"useless\" measurements with more useful ones, while still gathering the necessary information to construct $\\bar X$. In particular, group the GHZ qubits into pairs $(2k, 2k+1)$, each with a *check* qubit $c = 2k$ and a *root* qubit $r = 2k+1$. Because $X_cX_r$ and $Z_cZ_r$ commute, you can measure both. A $CX$ from $r$ to $c$ maps $X_cX_r \\to X_r$ and $Z_cZ_r \\to Z_c$, so afterward:\n"
msgstr "DisCo ED bermula daripada pemerhatian bahawa keadaan GHZ ialah kod ulangan: penstabilnya ialah $Z_jZ_{j+1}$ dan pengendali logiknya ialah $\\bar X$. Pengukuran bacaan biasa mengukur setiap qubit dalam asas $X$, yang mendedahkan $\\bar X$ tetapi dengan mengumpul maklumat bebas yang tidak berguna kepada protokol (iaitu, setiap $X$ individu). Idea DisCo ED ialah menggantikan pengukuran \"tidak berguna\" ini dengan yang lebih berguna, sambil tetap mengumpul maklumat yang diperlukan untuk membina $\\bar X$. Khususnya, kumpulkan qubit GHZ kepada pasangan $(2k, 2k+1)$, masing-masing dengan qubit *semakan* $c = 2k$ dan qubit *akar* $r = 2k+1$. Oleh sebab $X_cX_r$ dan $Z_cZ_r$ kalis tukar tertib, anda boleh mengukur kedua-duanya. Sebuah $CX$ daripada $r$ ke $c$ memetakan $X_cX_r \\to X_r$ dan $Z_cZ_r \\to Z_c$, jadi selepas itu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "the root, measured in the $X$ basis, gives bit $r_k$, the value of $X_cX_r$. The product of all root outcomes is $\\bar X$, so the herald is an odd number of 1s among the $r_k$.\n"
msgstr "akar, yang diukur dalam asas $X$, memberikan bit $r_k$, nilai $X_cX_r$. Hasil darab semua hasil akar ialah $\\bar X$, jadi isyaratnya ialah bilangan 1 yang ganjil dalam kalangan $r_k$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "the check, measured in the $Z$ basis, gives bit $f_k$, the value of the stabilizer $Z_cZ_r$. Without errors, $f_k = 0$.\n"
msgstr "semakan, yang diukur dalam asas $Z$, memberikan bit $f_k$, nilai penstabil $Z_cZ_r$. Tanpa ralat, $f_k = 0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This gives two variants.\n"
msgstr "Ini memberikan dua varian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Explicit check:** $CX(r\\to c)$, then $H$ on $r$. Reject the shot if any $f_k = 1$.\n"
msgstr "**Semakan eksplisit:** $CX(r\\to c)$, kemudian $H$ pada $r$. Tolak tembakan jika mana-mana $f_k = 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Implicit check:** add a second $CX(r\\to c)$ after the $H$. The root still gives $X_cX_r$, but the check now measures the product $X_cX_r \\cdot Z_cZ_r$, so without errors $f_k = r_k$. Reject the shot if any $f_k \\ne r_k$.\n"
msgstr "**Semakan tersirat:** tambah $CX(r\\to c)$ kedua selepas $H$. Akar masih memberikan $X_cX_r$, tetapi semakan kini mengukur hasil darab $X_cX_r \\cdot Z_cZ_r$, jadi tanpa ralat $f_k = r_k$. Tolak tembakan jika mana-mana $f_k \\ne r_k$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both variants check the same stabilizers. The difference is what happens when a readout error occurs on a root qubit: it flips the herald without touching any stabilizer, so the explicit check misses it, while the implicit check catches it because $f_k$ no longer matches $r_k$. The implicit readout $CX\\cdot H\\cdot CX$ compiles to the same single two-qubit gate as $CX\\cdot H$, so this extra protection costs no additional two-qubit gates.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua varian menyemak penstabil yang sama. Perbezaannya ialah apa yang berlaku apabila ralat bacaan berlaku pada qubit akar: ia membalikkan isyarat tanpa menyentuh mana-mana penstabil, jadi semakan eksplisit terlepas, manakala semakan tersirat mengesannya kerana $f_k$ tidak lagi sepadan dengan $r_k$. Bacaan tersirat $CX\\cdot H\\cdot CX$ dikompil kepada satu gate dua-qubit yang sama seperti $CX\\cdot H$, jadi perlindungan tambahan ini tidak memerlukan gate dua-qubit tambahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each pair is a detection patch of size $d = 2$. The paper also considers larger patches, which check more stabilizers at the cost of a deeper readout; this tutorial uses $d = 2$ throughout. With $d=2$, DisCo ED detects:\n"
msgstr "Setiap pasangan ialah tampalan pengesanan bersaiz $d = 2$. Kertas kerja itu juga mempertimbangkan tampalan yang lebih besar, yang menyemak lebih banyak penstabil dengan kos bacaan yang lebih dalam; tutorial ini menggunakan $d = 2$ sepanjang masa. Dengan $d=2$, DisCo ED mengesan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**any single bit flip on a GHZ qubit**, because every GHZ qubit belongs to exactly one checked pair.\n"
msgstr "**sebarang balikan bit tunggal pada qubit GHZ**, kerana setiap qubit GHZ tergolong dalam tepat satu pasangan yang disemak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**fusion errors**, provided the domain wall falls *inside* a pair. This is why the GHZ preparation, as shown below, uses the staggered patches $[0], [1,2], [3,4], \\ldots$: their boundaries $(0|1), (2|3), \\ldots$ lie inside the detection pairs $[0,1], [2,3], \\ldots$. If the prep patches were aligned with the pairs, every domain wall would fall *between* two pairs, where nothing is checked.\n"
msgstr "**ralat gabungan**, dengan syarat dinding domain jatuh *di dalam* sepasang. Inilah sebabnya penyediaan GHZ, seperti yang ditunjukkan di bawah, menggunakan tampalan berselang-seli $[0], [1,2], [3,4], \\ldots$: sempadannya $(0|1), (2|3), \\ldots$ terletak di dalam pasangan pengesanan $[0,1], [2,3], \\ldots$. Jika tampalan penyediaan sejajar dengan pasangan, setiap dinding domain akan jatuh *antara* dua pasangan, di mana tiada apa yang disemak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**readout errors on the root qubits**, with the implicit check only.\n"
msgstr "**ralat bacaan pada qubit akar**, dengan semakan tersirat sahaja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "DisCo ED does not detect phase flips on the GHZ qubits, or any error on the W qubits themselves, so postselection improves the state without making it perfect. The price is the fraction of shots discarded (the *acceptance rate* is less than 1) and one extra layer of two-qubit gates in the readout. No additional qubits are needed over the non-error detected implementation.\n"
msgstr "DisCo ED tidak mengesan balikan fasa pada qubit GHZ, atau sebarang ralat pada qubit W itu sendiri, jadi pascapemilihan memperbaik keadaan tanpa menjadikannya sempurna. Harganya ialah pecahan tembakan yang dibuang (*kadar penerimaan* kurang daripada 1) dan satu lapisan tambahan gate dua-qubit dalam bacaan. Tiada qubit tambahan diperlukan berbanding pelaksanaan tanpa pengesanan ralat.\n"

